  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A uniform rectangular thin sheet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> has length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and breadth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. If the shaded portion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>O</mi></math> is cut-off, the coordinates of the centre of mass of the remaining portion will be:<br /><br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4e9f9043-6f80-41f8-848d-e1168fef6d5a-image.png\" style=\"width: 295px; height: 200px;\" /></p>",
